-- title:
--   Hensel lifting of a simple residual root into the adic completion
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring, write $\mathfrak m_A$ for its maximal ideal, $\kappa(A)$ for its residue field and $\mathrm{res}\colon A \to \kappa(A)$ for the residue map, and let $\hat A =$ `AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A` be the $\mathfrak m_A$-adic completion of $A$, regarded as an $A$-algebra via its structure map $\iota =$ `algebraMap`. Let $P \in A[X]$ be monic, and let $r \in \kappa(A)$ satisfy $\bar P(r) = 0$ and $\bar P'(r) \neq 0$, where $\bar P$ denotes the image of $P$ in $\kappa(A)[X]$ under coefficientwise reduction and $\bar P'$ its formal derivative; that is, $r$ is a simple root of the reduction of $P$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an element $t \in \hat A$ and an element $a \in A$ such that the evaluation of $P$ at $t$ (via the $A$-algebra structure of $\hat A$) vanishes, $\mathrm{res}(a) = r$, and $t - \iota(a)$ lies in the ideal $\mathfrak m_A \hat A$ of $\hat A$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $\iota$. Thus the simple residual root $r$ lifts to an honest root of $P$ in the completion, congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A \hat A$ to a prescribed lift of $r$ in $A$.
--
--   This is Hensel's lemma for the adic completion of a Noetherian local ring, in the form needed to produce roots of a monic polynomial over $\hat A$ from simple roots over the residue field, with control on the residue class of the root. It is used in the construction of a ring homomorphism from a local ring into an adic completion under discrete-valuation hypotheses, via [`IsLocalRing.exists_ringHom_adicCompletion_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_residueField`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_ringHom_adicCompletion_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_map_of_residueField).
